            <ArticleTitle>Angiomyomatous Leiomyoma of a Female Urethral Meatus Recurrence After Seven Years of the Resection: A Case Report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>24-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.eucr.2016.08.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 20 years old woman had an external urethral orifice mass and received an excision operation. Seven years later, she complained a tumor with pain that was similar to the previous tumor. She underwent the tumor removal. Pathological diagnosis was a urethral angiomyomatous leiomyoma in the new concept of estrogen receptor-positive smooth muscle tumors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
